The implementation is complete and verified. Final summary:

## Delivered files

| file | contents |
|---|---|
| `/workspace/src/vk.zig` | the module (1144 lines) |
| `/workspace/src/vk_bindings.zig` | Vulkan declarations generated with `zig translate-c` from `vulkan/vulkan.h` (1.5 MB, self-contained, compiled and verified; no `@cImport`) |
| `/workspace/tools/vktest.zig` | smoke test / benchmark (built with `zig build-exe`, see `tools/build_vktest.sh`) |
| `/workspace/tools/add.comp`, `add.spv`, `push.comp`, `push.spv` | test shaders (storage buffers, push constants) |
| `/workspace/tools/buildtest/build.zig` | verified `build.zig` integration (Debug + ReleaseFast, runs with `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` unset via RUNPATH) |
| `/workspace/tools/VK_STATUS.md` | exact API, verified build.zig snippet, device/features, exact test output, measurements, limitations |

## API (all required signatures preserved)

```zig
pub const Buffer = struct { buffer, memory, size: u64, device_address: u64, host_visible: bool };
pub const Pipeline = struct { pipeline, layout, set_layout, descriptor_pool, descriptor_set,
                              storage_buffer_count: u32, push_constant_size: u32 };
pub const Vk = struct {
    pub fn init(alloc: std.mem.Allocator) !Vk;
    pub fn deinit(self: *Vk) void;
    pub fn deviceName(self: *const Vk) []const u8;
    pub fn uploadDeviceLocal(self: *Vk, data: []const u8) !Buffer;
    pub fn download(self: *Vk, buf: Buffer, out: []u8) !void;
    pub fn downloadRange(self: *Vk, buf: Buffer, offset: u64, out: []u8) !void;
    pub fn destroyBuffer(self: *Vk, buf: Buffer) void;
    pub fn createComputePipeline(self: *Vk, spirv: []const u32, n_storage_buffers: u32) !Pipeline;
    pub fn dispatch(self: *Vk, pipe: Pipeline, bufs: []const Buffer, gx: u32, gy: u32, gz: u32) !void;
    // extras
    pub fn createComputePipelineEx(..., push_constant_bytes: u32) !Pipeline;
    pub fn dispatchPush(..., push_data: []const u8, gx, gy, gz) !void;
    pub fn createDeviceBuffer / createHostBuffer / writeBuffer / mapHostBuffer / unmapHostBuffer / destroyPipeline;
    pub fn apiVersion / hasBufferDeviceAddress;
    // state: caps: Caps, exts, enabled_extensions, mem_props, limits, submit_count
};
```

## Measured results (AMD Radeon RX 9070 / RADV GFX1201, apiVersion 1.4.335)

- `Vk.init` (1.4 instance + first compute-queue device + queue + pool + fence): 10–22 ms.
- 512 MiB `uploadDeviceLocal` (staging + `vkCmdCopyBuffer` + fence): ~107 ms, ~5.0 GB/s; `device_address=0xffff800100200000` (BDA active).
- 1 MiB `download`: 3.4–9 ms; prefix, mid and tail markers verified, plus compute results element-wise.
- All 12 requested core features plus all 12 requested extension feature sets are advertised and enabled; 14 device extensions enabled (`VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix`, maintenance5/7/8/9, float_controls2, expect_assume, subgroup_rotate, maximal_reconvergence, quad_control, untyped_pointers, subgroup_uniform_control_flow, workgroup_memory_explicit_layout, robustness2).
- Compute dispatch (2 storage buffers, 4096 elems) and push-constant dispatch (4-byte block) both verified.
- With `VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation`: 0 validation errors/warnings. RADV's non-conformant warning is expected/ignored.

Key correctness details: feature/property structs are version-gated on the physical device API version; extension feature structs are chained only when the extension is advertised; `robustBufferAccess` is auto-enabled with `robustBufferAccess2` (fixes VUID-…-04000); absent optional features never fail init; instance falls back 1.4→1.3→1.2 only if the loader refuses. Calls are synchronous/single-threaded; caller owns buffer/pipeline lifetimes.
